# .gitignore
#
# WHY THIS FILE MATTERS MORE HERE THAN USUAL. Section 8 of the build document, mechanism 4:
# founder shaped output never enters a repo. This repository is private, but private is not
# the same as safe. A founder workspace holds 25 to 35 real people per founder, with names,
# companies, titles and email addresses, and none of those people agreed to be in a git
# history. A commit is forever, and a private repo can be shared, cloned, or made public by
# somebody who does not know what is in it.
#
# The content repo already gitignores /growth-engine/ for exactly this reason. Same rule,
# same reason, one level up.

# ---- Founder data. Nothing under here is ever committed. --------------------------------
/tmp/
/workspace/
# Anchored with a leading slash. Unanchored, this also matched vendor/growth-engine,
# which is the pinned content submodule and must be tracked. The content repo had the
# identical bug: it excluded the whole plugin from git and shipped an install with no ge.
/growth-engine/
/runs/
*.founder.json
backup/
*.tar.gz.enc

# ---- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.founderbrain.example
*.pem
*.key
!src/**/*.key.ts
secrets/

# ---- Probe output. Holds hostnames and boot markers, not secrets, but it is scratch. -----
.probe-state/
probe-report-*.txt

# ---- Build output -----------------------------------------------------------------------
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---- Dependencies -----------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# ---- Tooling and editors ----------------------------------------------------------------
coverage/
.vitest/
.eslintcache
.DS_Store
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.vscode/
.idea/

# ---- AI coding assistants ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Same rule as the founder data block at the top: none of this belongs in a git history.
#
# On this Replit box the separation is luck, not design. Claude Code keeps its credentials,
# session transcripts and project state under $HOME/.claude, and HOME is /home/runner while
# the repo is /home/runner/workspace. That is one `git init` in the wrong directory away
# from being wrong, and a laptop checkout has no such separation at all.
#
# What these files actually hold: OAuth tokens and API keys (.credentials.json,
# .claude.json, .codex/auth.json), full session transcripts including every file read and
# every command run (projects/, history.jsonl, sessions/), and shell snapshots that capture
# the environment. A transcript of work in a founder workspace contains founder data by
# construction, so it falls under mechanism 4 exactly like /workspace/ does.
#
# The patterns are deliberately unanchored: they match at the repo root AND in any
# subdirectory, because the failure mode is a tool writing state somewhere unexpected.

# Claude Code
.claude/
.claude.json
.claude.json.backup*
# If team-shared Claude config is ever wanted, un-ignore only the reviewable pieces, never
# the whole directory:
#   !.claude/settings.json      <- shared settings. NEVER settings.local.json.
#   !.claude/commands/
#   !.claude/agents/
#   !.claude/skills/
# CLAUDE.md at the repo root holds personal working instructions, not project docs, so it
# is ignored too. Anchored: only the root one, in case a subdir ever needs a tracked copy.
/CLAUDE.md

# OpenAI Codex CLI (codex), used here in an advisory role alongside Claude
.codex/
# auth.json holds the OAuth tokens or API key, sessions/ and history.jsonl hold full
# transcripts, and config.toml can carry MCP server definitions with API keys inline.
# Same un-ignore note as above if AGENTS.md-style shared config is ever worth committing.

# Antigravity CLI (agy). Despite the name it stores everything under .gemini/:
# conversations/, brain/, knowledge/, a conversation_summaries.db and OAuth credentials.
# Currently at $HOME/.gemini, outside the repo, but ignored here for the same reason as
# the rest of this block.
.gemini/
.antigravity/

# Anything else that wanders through
.aider*
.continue/
.windsurf/
.codeium/

# ---- Replit ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The workspace's own scratch. .replit and replit.nix ARE committed: they are the machine
# definition and the team needs them under review.
.replit.local
.config/
.upm/
.breakpoints
replit_zip_error_log.txt
# Machine state, including .cache/claude-cli-nodejs (MCP server logs). Replit's own
# /etc/.gitignore covers these via core.excludesFile, but that is a property of this box,
# not of this repo, and it does not travel with a clone. Repeated here so it does.
.cache/
.local/
.agents/memory/
